Vendored copy of dumbpipe, built from source by the fs-portal Dockerfile so
we do not depend on upstream's mutable release binaries.

Upstream:  https://github.com/n0-computer/dumbpipe
Tag:       v0.39.0
Source:    https://github.com/n0-computer/dumbpipe/archive/refs/tags/v0.39.0.tar.gz
sha256:    89d01b0b6d25fc8baf06ab791fd0a2b35b24ac51d0bd01b64d36c35750aaf3e9
License:   MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-MIT / LICENSE-APACHE alongside)
Vendored:  2026-08-15; contents are the tag's src/, tests/, Cargo.toml,
           Cargo.lock, licenses and README. .github/ and .gitignore
           omitted. Dependencies are pinned by the committed Cargo.lock
           (built with --locked).

Local patches (kept minimal; re-apply when upgrading):
  * src/main.rs: `--max-connections <N>` flag on `listen-tcp` and
    `connect-tcp` (default 0 = unlimited, upstream behavior). A tokio
    semaphore caps how many connections are forwarded concurrently; extra
    connections queue until a slot frees instead of erroring. fs-portal
    uses it to enforce FSP_MAX_STREAMS on both the export and import side.
    Exercised by test/integration/run.sh (stream-cap checks).
  * src/metrics.rs (new file) + src/main.rs: observability. Process-wide
    forwarding counters (connections total/active/closed, bytes per
    direction, errors, queue waits, stream duration) exposed as Prometheus
    text on the address in DUMBPIPE_METRICS_ADDR (unset = disabled) via a
    dependency-free std HTTP thread — Cargo.lock unchanged. The copy loops
    are instrumented: per-stream "stream start"/"stream closed" logs with
    byte totals and average MiB/s, plus a per-32MiB chunk speed log line.
    Cargo tests live in src/metrics.rs; scraped by
    test/integration/run.sh (metrics checks).

To upgrade: fetch a newer tag tarball, verify its sha256, replace these
files wholesale, re-apply the local patches above, update this file, and
re-run tools/fs-portal/test.sh (the build gate runs upstream's cargo tests
via the dumbpipe-test stage).
